    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d664">

                <pb facs="0813" n="689" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg689"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/2086: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-04-18T10:00:00-05:29"><hi rendition="#italic">April 18,
                                1921—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 7:13
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>69. Statement forwarded in your telegram 97, April 16, 11 a.m., was given to
                    press April 17, 2 p.m., three minor verbal changes being made therein. After
                    Department’s telegram 98 had been <pb facs="0814" n="690" xml:id="pg690"/>
                    carefully considered by General Crowder and me statement was published in <hi
                        rendition="#italic">La Noche</hi> of last night and in today’s morning
                    papers.</p>
                <p>The press also carried statement by General Gómez to his party in which he
                    recommends acceptance of defeat rather than endanger the safety of the Republic
                    by another American intervention and announces his intention to retire to
                    private life. Clippings of statements will follow in next pouch.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
